# 2026-10-20 Qwen3 0.6B on the CPU (lane lu1020, round r1), Android, one sitting per device (after a cooling hold; the
# GPU rows are matrices/lu1020-q06-gpu-a-android.cells and -gpu-b-android.cells): the current Hub file
# Qwen3-0.6B_dynamic_wi4b32_afp32.litertlm (litert-community/Qwen3-0.6B main e6687177, lfs sha256 03e7da1e…2856,
# 344,671,744 B) on the CPU with XNNPACK and with YNNPACK, the two arms of ONE binary: the side build
# head-lm2ef6baeb-rtd469ea48-xnn878f1d8c-ynn-cpuonly (android/engine-pins.json; litert_lm_main + litert_lm_advanced_main
# built at LiteRT-LM main 2ef6baeb with LiteRT main d469ea48 by --override_repository=litert=<clone>, both the heads of
# 2026-10-20 15:5x JST, XNNPACK 878f1d8c and slinky 9b2ee975 by --override_repository (the pins of LiteRT d469ea48's
# litert_workspace.bzl; LiteRT-LM's WORKSPACE takes XNNPACK 0a66ebb5 and slinky a3eec6fc from TensorFlow's
# workspace), --define=litert_enable_ynnpack=true, without which LiteRT links no YNNPACK accelerator, and
# --@litert//litert/build_common:build_include=cpu_only: LiteRT d469ea48 with its GPU code does not get through the
# analysis inside LiteRT-LM 2ef6baeb's workspace (its GPU code needs ML Drift, whose repositories LiteRT-LM does not
# define), and the CPU rows need no GPU; + the commit's prebuilt libGemmaModelConstraintProvider.so), in
# /data/local/tmp/llmbench/engines/<that tag>/;
# the flat pinned v0.18.0 build is not touched. ynnpack=1 = --enable_ynnpack=true (arm litert-lm-cpu-ynnpack); the
# rows without it are the XNNPACK arm (litert-lm-cpu) of the same binary, and the payload interleaves the two per
# round. Not page rows: the model id is the Mac catalog id of the same Hub file, so the rows stay apart from the
# page's v0.18.0 rows (litert-community/Qwen3-0.6B + file=), and file= is the file's path in the host's Hub cache
# (pushed as it is, sha256-checked on the phone: the record's model.sha256). First row = the Android session anchor
# of matrices/dashboard-text-v1.cells. Short-chat is no CPU row here: the team's CPU rows are the 1K task and the
# protocol.
#   BENCH_SITTING=1 python3 scripts/dashboard_job.py s26 --cells matrices/lu1020-q06-cpu-android.cells --suffix lu1020-cpu --once --hold-held-by <keeper pid> --no-page-commit
#   BENCH_SITTING=1 python3 scripts/dashboard_job.py pixel8a --cells matrices/lu1020-q06-cpu-android.cells --suffix lu1020-cpu --once --hold-held-by <keeper pid> --no-page-commit

